{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789251683,"nonce":"tVDS+Vhz8we/scNXrKiQi22lZ7k=","title":"Hosted wren_lift: a compiled loop that never allocates never reaches a stop","message":"A tiered wren_lift loop with no allocation in its body never polls\nshould_collect, so a stop requested by another mutator waits out the\ncore's rendezvous deadline and is abandoned. Single-resident processes\nare unaffected (nothing else requests stops).\n\nFix on wren_lift's side: a poll on JIT back-edges, or its poll-request\nhook wired to the core's POLL_EPOCH the way ash's compiled loops are.\nSame shape as the scheduler's preemption epoch; the seam gains a slot for\nthe epoch address. Blocks a world with wren_lift and another resident\nthat collects.","files":null}]}